id: 13
hanzi: 尾巴
pinyin: wěi ba
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: tail (of animal, aircraft, comet); rear end; shadow or follower
  es: cola; rabo; extremidad posterior; parte final o rastro

senses[2]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | the flexible appendage extending from the rear of an animal's body; the posterior end of an object | apéndice articulado en la parte posterior del cuerpo de los animales; extremo trasero | 摇尾巴 (wag the tail)
  2 | Noun | Colloquial | a person tracking, tailing, or shadowing someone from behind | persona que sigue o vigila a otra de cerca; rastro o cola | 甩掉尾巴 (shake off a tail/tracker)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 小狗看见主人推门进屋，立刻兴奋地飞奔过来，欢快地不停摇晃着毛茸茸的尾巴。 | Xiǎogǒu kànjiàn zhǔrén tuīmén jìnwū, lìkè xīngfèn de fēibēn guòlái, huānkuài de bùtíng yáohuàng zhe máorōngrōng de wěiba. | Seeing its owner push open the door and enter, the puppy immediately bounded over excitedly, joyfully wagging its fluffy tail without stopping. | Al ver a su dueño abrir la puerta y entrar, el perrito corrió entusiasmado hacia él, moviendo sin cesar su peluda cola con alegría.
  #2 | 摸象的第四个盲人抓住了大象细长的尾巴，便十分确信地大喊大象其实就像一根粗糙的绳子。 | Mō xiàng de dì sì gè mángrén zhuāzhù le dàxiàng xìcháng de wěiba, biàn shífēn quèxìn de dàhǎn dàxiàng qíshí jiù xiàng yì gēn cūcāo de shéngzi. | The fourth blind man grabbed the elephant's slender tail and shouted with absolute certainty that an elephant was actually like a coarse rope. | El cuarto ciego asió la delgada cola del elefante y gritó con total convicción que el animal se asemejaba exactamente a una soga áspera.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  摇尾巴 | wag the tail
  翘尾巴 | get cocky; become conceited
  夹着尾巴 | with tail between one's legs; humbled
  大象尾巴 | elephant's tail
  长长的尾巴 | long tail
  彗星尾巴 | tail of a comet

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  尾大不掉 | wěi dà bù diào | the tail is too big to wag; subordinate too strong to manage
  虎头蛇尾 | hǔ tóu shé wěi | tiger's head and snake's tail; start with a flourish but end weakly
  藏头露尾 | cáng tóu lù wěi | hide head and expose tail; act slyly and deceitfully
  畏首畏尾 | wèi shǒu wèi wěi | fear head and fear tail; excessively timid and hesitant

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  尾 | wěi | tail; rear; end; stern | cola; rabo; extremo | 尸 | corpse / body frame | 尸 (human bent torso) | 毛 (máo, hair / fur) | 7 | 半包围结构 | Ancient oracle bone pictogram showing a human body 尸 wearing a long hairy tail 毛 hanging from behind. | From behind the rear of the physical body (尸) hangs a long strand of animal fur (毛), forming a tail (尾). | Tras la silueta del cuerpo (尸) desciende un mechón de pelo y cerdas (毛), dibujando la cola (尾). | 214 | SHFU | 
  巴 | bā | cling to; eager; crust; tail suffix | adherir; anhelar; sufijo nominal | 巳 | sixth earthly branch | 巳 (curled snake / serpent) | "" | 4 | 单一结构 | Ancient bronze pictogram of a giant coiled python or serpent with its tail hooked upward. | A giant creeping serpent curves its scaly body and hooks its tail upward with tenacity (巴). | Una serpiente gigante enrosca su cuerpo con el rabo curvado hacia lo alto con tenacidad (巴). | 55 | AU | 

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Animal hair trailing behind the body (尾) curves tenaciously like a snake (巴) to form an animal's expressive tail (尾巴).
  composite_memory_hook_es: El pelaje tras el cuerpo (尾) que se curva como una sierpe (巴) da forma a la cola (尾巴).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: The character 尾 dates back to ancient sacrificial dancers who tied animal tails to their hips. In modern Mandarin, 巴 functions as a phonetic nominalizing suffix (as in 嘴巴, 下巴, 尾巴). Figuratively, 尾巴 symbolizes concealable flaws or overconfidence (夹着尾巴做人, 尾巴翘上天).
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Dipping 3rd tone followed by neutral tone: 'wěi ba' (214-neutral). Pronounce 'wěi' fully, then deliver 'ba' with a light, unstressed release.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[5]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
