    把 | bǎ | hold; grasp; handle
    爸 | bà | father; dad
    疤 | bā | scar; scab
    耙 | pá | rake; harrow

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 尾巴 is the full colloquial and anatomical noun for an animal's tail or rear trail, whereas 尾 alone is used in compound morphemes.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 尾巴 vs. 尾 | wěi | 尾巴 is the standalone spoken and written noun for a tail (狗尾巴), whereas 尾 is a bound morpheme in compounds and formal written phrases (车尾, 结尾, 年尾).
    2 | 尾巴 vs. 后端 | hòuduān | 尾巴 is concrete and biological or figurative for a tracker, whereas 后端 is technical and spatial, used for engineering, software backends, or structural rear ends.
    3 | 尾巴 vs. 痕迹 | hénjì | 尾巴 describes a physical extension or tracker, while 痕迹 refers to left-behind impressions, footprints, or abstract traces of past events.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 在广袤的大自然中，动物的尾巴具有极其奇妙的生理功能。鸟类的尾巴在翱翔中调节平衡，袋鼠的尾巴宛如强有力的第三条腿，而松鼠蓬松的尾巴则在凛冽寒冬中化作温暖的毛毯。大自然造物的精巧令人叹为观止。 | Zài guǎngmào de dàzìrán zhōng, dòngwù de wěiba jùyǒu jíqí qímiào de shēnglǐ gōngnéng. Niǎolèi de wěiba zài áoxiáng zhōng tiáojié pínghéng, dàishǔ de wěiba wǎnrú qiángyǒulì de dì-sān tiáo tuǐ, ér sōngshǔ péngsōng de wěiba zé zài lǐnliè hándōng zhōng huàzuò wēnnuǎn de máotǎn. Dàzìrán zàowù de jīngqiǎo lìng rén tànwéiguānzhǐ. | In vast nature, animal tails possess marvelous physiological adaptations. A bird's tail regulates balance during flight, a kangaroo's tail acts as a powerful third leg, and a squirrel's fluffy tail becomes a cozy blanket in winter. The ingenuity of creation is breathtaking. | En la vasta naturaleza, las colas de los animales desempeñan admirables funciones biológicas. Las aves equilibran su vuelo con ellas, el canguro las usa como un tercer pie y la ardilla las convierte en mullida manta invernal. El prodigio de la creación animal colma de asombro.
  #2 | 在管理心理学中，“翘尾巴”常被用来警示团队在取得阶段性成绩后滋生的盲目自满。保持谦逊谨慎的清醒头脑，杜绝麻痹大意，才能在日趋激烈的市场竞争中行稳致远，避免重蹈虎头蛇尾的覆辙。 | Zài guǎnlǐ xīnlǐxué zhōng, 'qiào wěiba' cháng bèi yònglái jǐngshì tuánduì zài qǔdé jiēduànxìng chéngjì hòu zīshēng de mángmù zìmǎn. Bǎochí qiānxùn jǐnshèn de qīngxǐng tóunǎo, dùjué mábì dàyì, cáinéng zài rìqū jīliè de shìchǎng jìngzhēng zhōng xíngwěn-zhìyuǎn, bìmǐan chóngdǎo hǔtóu-shéwěi de fùzhé. | In management psychology, 'raising one's tail' warns against complacency following initial victories. Maintaining humble lucidity and rooting out carelessness allows an organization to advance steadily in fierce competition, avoiding the pitfall of beginning well but ending poorly. | En la psicología directiva, la advertencia de no ufanarse previene la autocomplacencia tras un éxito inicial. Mantener la prudencia y la mente despierta permite navegar con paso firme en mercados voraces, evitando el descalabro de empezar con bríos y fenecer con desgana.
